From: HarmonyOS PC Porting <porting@example.com>
Date: Mon, 18 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Fix bits/types/FILE.h include for musl libc

intercept.h includes <bits/types/FILE.h> under #ifdef __linux__.
This header is glibc-internal and does not exist in musl libc
(used by OHOS). The FILE type is provided by <stdio.h> in musl.

Guard the glibc-specific include with __GLIBC__ and fall back to
<stdio.h> on musl-based systems.

--- a/src/interceptor/intercept.h
+++ b/src/interceptor/intercept.h
@@ -27,8 +27,12 @@
 #define _GNU_SOURCE 1
 #endif
 
-#ifdef __linux__
+/* On glibc, bits/types/FILE.h provides the FILE type definition.
+ On musl (including OHOS), <stdio.h> provides FILE. */
+#if defined(__linux__) && defined(__GLIBC__)
 #include <bits/types/FILE.h>
+#else
+#include <stdio.h>
 #endif
 
 #include <dlfcn.h>
